## 2. Nearby Attractions (within 20 km)

| Attraction | Distance | Highlights | Suggested Visit Time |
|------------|----------|------------|----------------------|
| **St. Mark’s Square (Piazza San Marco)** | 12 km | St. Mark’s Basilica, Campanile, Doge’s Palace | 2–3 h |
| **Rialto Bridge & Market** | 12 km | Iconic bridge, fish market, souvenir stalls | 1–2 h |
| **Peggy Guggenheim Collection** | 12 km | Modern art museum on the Grand Canal | 1.5 h |
| **Murano Island** | 20 km (boat) | Glass‑blowing workshops, artisan shops | 4–5 h (day trip) |
| **Burano Island** | 20 km (boat) | Colorful houses, lace‑making | 4–5 h (day trip) |

> *All are reachable by train, bus, or a short taxi ride.*

---

## 3. Suggested Sightseeing Routes

| Route | Duration | Highlights | How to Get There |
|-------|----------|------------|------------------|
| **Venice City Centre Loop** | 1 day | St. Mark’s Square → Doge’s Palace → Rialto Bridge → Grand Canal | Train from airport → *Venezia Santa Lucia* → walk |
| **Canal Tour** | 2–3 h | Grand Canal, Rialto, Dorsoduro, San Giorgio Maggiore | Vaporetto (water bus) or private gondola |
| **Murano & Burano Day Trip** | 1 day | Glass‑blowing in Murano, lace in Burano | Ferry from Venice (≈30 min each) |
| **Lido Beach & Film Festival Site** | 1 day | Lido beach, historic cinema | Train to Lido (≈20 min) or bus |
| **Venice & Verona Combo** | 2 days | Venice city centre + Verona’s Arena & Juliet’s balcony | Train from Venice to Verona (≈1 h) and back |

> **Tip:** Buy a *Venice Transport & Sightseeing* day pass (includes vaporetto, train, and some museum entries) for convenience and savings.

---

## 4. Practical Tips

| Topic | Recommendation |
|-------|----------------|
| **Weather (Nov)** | Cool (10–15 °C), possible rain – bring a light jacket and umbrella. |
| **Currency** | Euro (€). Credit cards accepted everywhere; keep some cash for small vendors. |
| **Dining** | Try cicchetti (Venetian tapas) in local bacari (wine bars). |
| **Safety** | Venice can be crowded; keep an eye on belongings, especially in tourist hotspots. |
| **Tickets** | Book major attractions (Doge’s Palace, Peggy Guggenheim) online in advance to skip lines. |

---

